    [
      m('How Long Does a Personal Injury Lawsuit Take From Start to Finish?', ['start to finish','usually take','timeline'], 'The easiest way to understand timing is to break the case into phases instead of asking for one single number. Intake and investigation may take days to a few weeks, treatment and case development can take weeks or months, pre-suit negotiation can take weeks to months, and litigation can add many more months if the case does not settle early.', ['Initial investigation and intake', 'Medical treatment and case development', 'Demand and pre-suit negotiation', 'Lawsuit filing and discovery', 'Mediation or renewed settlement talks', 'Trial preparation and trial'], ['Anyone gives you one exact number without explaining the phase that is still unknown']),
      m('What Happens During Each Phase of a Personal Injury Case', ['what happens after i sign','what happens'], 'After you sign, the usual next steps are investigation, records collection, insurance notice, treatment tracking, and claim-building. If the case does not settle pre-suit, the timeline shifts into filing, discovery, motions, negotiation, and possibly trial preparation.', ['Confirm what records or documents they need first', 'Ask what can delay the timeline', 'Ask when a demand usually goes out', 'Ask what changes if the case must be filed'], ['No one can explain the next stage after intake']),
      m('When Should You Talk to a Lawyer After an Accident?', ['when should i talk'], 'It usually helps to talk to a lawyer before recorded statements, early settlement pressure, or deadline confusion turn a simple claim into a mess. Early contact matters most when fault is disputed, injuries are getting clearer over time, or the insurer is already pushing for quick statements or releases.', ['Talk early if the insurer is asking for a recorded statement', 'Talk early if liability is disputed', 'Talk early if treatment is still unfolding'], ['You wait until after signing a release to ask bigger questions']),
      m('How Long Does Settlement Negotiation Usually Last?', ['settlement negotiation'], 'Settlement negotiation can be short or drawn out depending on treatment status, fault disputes, and whether the insurer believes the case may actually be filed. A negotiation timeline only makes sense when you know what stage the case is in and what information is still missing.', ['Ask whether the case is still missing treatment records', 'Ask what usually triggers a real insurer response', 'Ask what changes if pre-suit negotiation stalls'], ['They discuss negotiation timing without explaining treatment or evidence gaps'])
    ]
